When implementing or changing behaviour covered by an FS/AD, **read the relevant doc first** and keep code aligned with it.

Additional copies may exist under `docs/specifications/` and `docs/architecture/` — prefer `/docs` as the agent-facing canonical path unless the user specifies otherwise.

### Spec section standard (FS)

Feature Specifications should include, as applicable:

- Problem Statement
- Business Goals
- User Stories
- Functional Requirements
- SmartAssist Behaviour
- UX Design
- Reality First Principle
- Persistence / Ownership Rules
- Acceptance Criteria

Architecture Decisions (AD) should include: Decision, Rationale, Requirements, Consequences, Compliance tests.

## Engineering defaults

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Do not invent data to make UI look complete
- Filtered collections must follow **AD-001 Filter Transparency**
- Opportunity people live on the opportunity roster and reference Contact Registry IDs — never invent contacts
- Match existing TypeScript / React / design-system patterns in `src/`
- Do not commit unless the user asks
- Do not push unless the user asks

## Next.js note

This project may use a Next.js version with breaking changes. Before writing Next.js-specific code, check `AGENTS.md` and `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when relevant.
